cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this instrument or its calibration reports, please cite the archived record."
type: software
title: "Exact-null dependence metrology for parallel decoders"
abstract: >-
  A calibrated instrument for measuring the statistical dependence a parallel or
  masked decoder destroys or manufactures, against nulls that are exactly zero by
  construction. Ships two exact nulls (a covariance-sparse epsilon-biased field
  with exact marginal independence off-graph, and a precision-sparse Gaussian
  Markov random field with exact conditional independence across separators), a
  continuous coupling dial with an exact feasible window, per-edge hypothesis
  tests with family-wise error control, and the ParallelBench Theorem-1 floor as
  comparator. Includes the nominal-token adaptation and closed-form
  Hermite-spectrum edge target required to run the same estimators in a
  vector-quantized image token space. Two calibration gates are archived with
  their reports: GM1 (core, 2026-07-26) and GM1-VQ (image-VQ token space,
  aMUSEd-256, 2026-07-27), both passed, both reproducing bit-identically.
authors:
